# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# Compiled binary (from go build)
/server
/bin/

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.production

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.cache
.gocache

# Media files
uploads/

# Build artifacts
tmp/

# Renders from cmd/zz_model_compare: real images, judged by eye, not repository content.
model-compare/

# The compiled throwaway commands. `go build ./cmd/zz_...` drops a binary here
# and a `git add -A backend` sweeps it into a commit.
#
# A pattern, not a list. This named zz_model_compare specifically, on the
# reasoning that every other rule in this file names a thing too -- and four
# commits later zz_reference_run was written, built, and committed at 79 MB,
# because a list only covers what existed when it was written. Every command
# under cmd/zz_ is a throwaway by that prefix, so the prefix is the rule.
/zz_*
